BT 1 0 0 1 0 108.112 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (The man.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Aurelius Augustinus, born 13 November 354 in Thagaste, in what is now Algeria.) Tj T* (His father Patricius was a town councillor, not a Christian until the end of his life, and) Tj T* (permanently short of money. His mother Monica was a Christian who did not let go.) Tj T* (Augustine was clever, ambitious, and being educated at cost towards a career as a) Tj T* (professional public speaker. He wrote this book in his early forties, around 397 to 400, about) Tj T* (twenty-five years after the events in this part, and only a couple of years into being a bishop.) Tj T* ET
