BT 1 0 0 1 0 108.112 Tm -0.087009 Tw 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (The argument of Book One.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Augustine started his life story before his own memory, and said) Tj T* 0 Tw (openly that his account of infancy came from watching other people\222s babies rather than from) Tj T* -0.01632 Tw (recall. He watched a speechless infant go pale with fury at another baby feeding beside it, and) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.001533 Tw (built a case on it: the baby has learned nothing, the milk is not scarce, and it rages anyway, so) Tj T* 0 Tw (whatever produces the rage was there on arrival. Book One ends with his lifelong formula.) Tj T* (The gifts were good. The aim was wrong. Evil is not a thing; it is a direction.) Tj T* ET
