BT 1 0 0 1 0 128.064 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (Book Seven, which matters most here.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Someone gave him books of the Platonists in Latin) Tj T* (translation, and they broke the assumption that had trapped him: that anything real must be) Tj T* (made of stuff. Once that went, the answer arrived. Evil is not a substance at all. It is a) Tj T* /F6 11.6 Tf (privation) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf (, a missing good in something that ought to have had it, and a bad will is not aimed) Tj T* (at something bad but has given a lower good the place belonging to a higher one. He also) Tj T* (turned inward and glimpsed something above his own mind, in what he calls the flash of one) Tj T* (trembling glance.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
