BT 1 0 0 1 0 28.304 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (The book.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( ) Tj /F5 11.6 Tf (Confessio) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( means three things at once: confessing sin, confessing faith, and) Tj T* (confessing praise. This is a prayer, addressed to God throughout, and you are overhearing it.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.52756 443.0303 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 108.112 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (The story so far.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Nine years with the Manichees, a religion teaching two eternal powers of) Tj T* (Light and Darkness. It collapsed. He drifted through scepticism to Milan, where the bishop) Tj T* (Ambrose showed him that scripture could be read figuratively. Books of the Platonists then) Tj T* -0.15729 Tw (broke the assumption that had trapped him \227 that anything real must be made of stuff \227 and) Tj T* 0 Tw (once that went he could accept that evil is not a substance but a ) Tj /F5 11.6 Tf (privation) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf (, a missing good in) Tj T* (something that ought to have had it.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.52756 296.8663 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 128.064 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (Book Eight, which this part follows directly.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Having the answer turned out not to be the) Tj T* (same as being able to live in it. Book Eight is about a man who is certain and cannot move. It) Tj T* (is built out of other people\222s stories \227 Victorinus, Antony in the Egyptian desert, two imperial) Tj T* -0.062936 Tw (agents at Trier \227 before it reaches his own. In a garden in Milan in the late summer of 386 he) Tj T* 0 Tw (heard a voice from a neighbouring house telling him to take up and read, opened the letters) Tj T* (of Paul at random, read four lines, and stopped arguing. Alypius read the next line and joined) Tj T* (him. They went indoors and told Monica.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 59.52756 150.7023 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 128.064 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (Two threads run in.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( The first is the woman. In Book Six the partner he had lived with for) Tj T* (over a decade, and whom he never names, was sent back to Africa so that he could make an) Tj T* (advantageous marriage. He took another woman while waiting. The engagement is still) Tj T* -0.053295 Tw (standing when Book Eight ends. The second is grief. In Book Four a friend died and Augustine) Tj T* 0 Tw (was destroyed by it, and the older man writing the book judges that grief a fault: the natural) Tj T* -0.035195 Tw (consequence of having loved a mortal thing as though it were permanent. Part Three said that) Tj T* 0 Tw (Book Nine is where he has to live with his own verdict. It is.) Tj T* ET
