BT 1 0 0 1 0 88.16 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (The man.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Born 354 in Roman North Africa, educated at his family\222s expense towards a career) Tj T* (as a professional public speaker. By 384 he held the public chair of rhetoric in Milan. He) Tj T* (resigned it in 386, was baptised in 387, went home to Africa, and was made a priest at Hippo) Tj T* (in 391 and a bishop about four years after that. He wrote this book in his early forties, around) Tj T* (397 to 400.) Tj T* ET
