q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 68.208 Tm 19.952 TL /F6 11.6 Tf .129412 .117647 .098039 rg (Three. The last debt in this series is paid here.) Tj /F1 11.6 Tf ( Part One promised Wittgenstein on) Tj T* (Augustine, treating him as a serious philosopher rather than as an example of error. Chapter) Tj T* (Nine pays it, and the first thing it has to do is separate that from the much more famous) Tj T* (passage where Wittgenstein does exactly the opposite.) Tj T* ET
